  "prefLabel": "Ins 204.06 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 204.06 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings. Unless called as witnesses or granted intervenor status, a complainant shall have no role during enforcement or disciplinary hearings beyond the role of witness or intervenor.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
